## Task fidelity and package relationships

The visible task is still to recognize one complete list of four binomial-times-
trinomial products for I-IV. In I, A/B/D show `(a+5)(a^2+13a+43)`, but C now
shows `(a+5)(a^2+a+43)`. Thus I is no longer unanimous, and the option set now
contains an actual mathematical distinction for source 317a.

B matches A in I, II and IV and differs only in III: its binomial is `x+7`
instead of `x-1`, with the same trinomial `x^2+10x+37`. Rejecting C or D from
another row therefore cannot distinguish A from B. Source 317c cannot be
bypassed via the other rows. Complete-table recognition and valid elimination
remain acceptable; this is not evidence of independently producing four written
factorizations.

The new visible row does not supply a correctness label or an answer cue.
Distinct coefficients require algebraic judgment. These conclusions do not
