## Changed-row calculation, before key disclosure

Using `u=a+6`, the cube-difference identity gives
`(u-1)(u^2+u+1)=(a+5)(a^2+13a+43)`.
C instead omits `12a` from the trinomial. Its expanded product is
`a^3+6a^2+48a+215`, whereas `(a+6)^3-1` is
`a^3+18a^2+108a+215`; original minus C is `12a(a+5)`.
At `a=1`, the original is `7^3-1=342`, while C gives `6*45=270`.
The omitted term creates a genuinely false alternative, not an equivalent
factorization.

This is the finite changed-row check, not a new solution pass over source 317
or the entire N20 package. The remaining option mathematics and capacity losses
will be received from the authorized inherited review.
